# Tests

Unit tests mock the database. Integration and end-to-end tests use `DATABASE_URL` on a database that can be wiped, never production.

A test that inserts rows uses `TestDataCleanup` from `tests/utils/testCleanup.ts`. Cleanup still runs when the test fails. Track every row created:

- `trackUser`, `trackCountry`, `trackCurrency`, `trackServiceProvider`
- `trackSubscription`, `trackSubscriptionSlot`, `trackSubscriptionRequest`, `trackCapacityAlert`

`cleanupAll` deletes alerts, subscriptions (and their slots and requests), providers, countries, currencies, then users. Prefer `getOrCreateTestUser`, `getOrCreateTestCountry`, `getOrCreateTestServiceProvider`, and `getOrCreateTestCurrency`.

Use a unique email or code. Do not assert that the database is empty; seed rows may remain.

```typescript
it(
  "creates a user and removes it",
  withTestCleanup(async (cleanup) => {
    const user = await cleanup.getOrCreateTestUser(`seat-${Date.now()}@example.com`);
    expect(user.isVerified).toBe(true);
  })
);
```
